{%- comment -%}
  PDP gallery: thumbnail rail + stage + mobile dot rail, for EVERY media type.

  Why it moved out of the section: both loops in the stage were guarded on
  media_type == 'image', so a merchant who uploaded a product video got a PDP
  that silently dropped it — the media was in the admin, paid for, and
  unreachable on the storefront. Video, external video and 3D preview stills now
  all render, in the merchant's own media order.

  THE JS CONTRACT (theme.js initPDP + pdp-extras.js initGalleryHeightSync read
  these; renaming any of them breaks the gallery, the colour jump and the zoom):
    .pdp__rail / .pdp__thumb[data-thumb-target=<media.id>][data-colors]
    .pdp__gallery
    .gallery-item[data-media-id][data-colors], .is-current on exactly one
    .gallery-item[data-zoom-src]  — the ZOOMABLE set. theme.js filters on this
      attribute, so video items must NOT carry it: a video in the zoom
      lightbox would open as a still frame with no controls.
    [data-gallery-dots] — theme.js builds and syncs the dot spans itself and
      hides the rail when fewer than two slides are visible, which is why this
      renders empty and [hidden]. It was simply never emitted before, so the
      mobile carousel had no position indicator at all while the code that
      draws one sat unused in theme.js.
    [data-gallery-counter] — the aria-live position cue.

  THE LCP CONTRACT with layout/theme.liquid: that file preloads
  product.featured_media at 500/640/800/1024, width only, no height, no crop,
  sizes "(max-width: 720px) 80vw, 46vw". The <img> below MUST mirror those four
  URLs and that sizes string byte for byte or the CDN hands back a different
  variant and the hero downloads twice. The eager image is chosen by MEDIA ID,
  not by loop position: featured_media is not always media[0], and matching on
  forloop.first meant the preloaded file was the one marked loading="lazy"
  while a different photo raced it for bandwidth.

  Params: product · color_opt_index · color_values
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign gal_count = product.media.size

  comment
    Which image the browser has already been told to fetch. A featured VIDEO
    leaves the layout's preload unwritten (it is guarded on media_type), so the
    first still in the set takes the eager slot instead — otherwise every slide
    is lazy and the stage paints last.
  endcomment
  assign lcp_media_id = 0
  if product.featured_media.media_type == 'image'
    assign lcp_media_id = product.featured_media.id
  else
    for gal_m in product.media
      if gal_m.media_type == 'image'
        assign lcp_media_id = gal_m.id
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif
-%}

<div class="pdp__stage">
  {%- if gal_count > 1 -%}
    <div class="pdp__rail" role="group" aria-label="{{ 'product.gallery.aria' | t }}">
      {%- for media in product.media -%}
        {%- capture thumb_colors -%}{%- render 'pdp-media-colors', media: media, product: product, color_opt_index: color_opt_index, color_values: color_values -%}{%- endcapture -%}
        {%- assign thumb_colors = thumb_colors | strip -%}
        {%- assign is_moving = false -%}
        {%- if media.media_type == 'video' or media.media_type == 'external_video' -%}{%- assign is_moving = true -%}{%- endif -%}
        <button
          type="button"
          class="pdp__thumb{% if is_moving %} pdp__thumb--video{% endif %}"
          data-thumb-target="{{ media.id }}"
          {% if thumb_colors != blank %}data-colors="{{ thumb_colors | escape }}"{% endif %}
          aria-label="{% if is_moving %}{{ 'product.form.show_video' | t }}{% else %}{{ 'product.gallery.show_image' | t: index: forloop.index }}{% endif %}"
        >
          {%- comment -%} image_url on a media object always resolves to its preview
          image, so one call covers stills, video posters and 3D previews. 128 =
          2x the 64px rail the stylesheet draws; the 3x step is there for the
          phone rail, where the same thumbs are the only navigation. {%- endcomment -%}
          <img
            src="{{ media | image_url: width: 128 }}"
            srcset="{{ media | image_url: width: 128 }} 1x, {{ media | image_url: width: 192 }} 1.5x, {{ media | image_url: width: 256 }} 2x"
            width="64" height="96" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt=""
          >
          {%- if is_moving -%}<span class="pdp__thumb-play" aria-hidden="true"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M8 5.5v13l11-6.5z"/></svg></span>{%- endif -%}
        </button>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  <div class="pdp__frame">
    <div class="pdp__gallery">
      {%- for media in product.media -%}
        {%- capture media_colors -%}{%- render 'pdp-media-colors', media: media, product: product, color_opt_index: color_opt_index, color_values: color_values -%}{%- endcapture -%}
        {%- assign media_colors = media_colors | strip -%}

        {%- case media.media_type -%}
          {%- when 'video' -%}
            {%- comment -%} A <div>, not the <button> the stills use: a <video controls>
            inside a button is unoperable — every click on play/scrub is swallowed by
            the button's activation. No data-zoom-src either, see the contract above.
            preload="none" keeps a 20MB clip off the critical path; the poster comes
            from image_size, so the slide is never an empty black box. {%- endcomment -%}
            <div
              class="gallery-item gallery-item--video{% if forloop.first %} is-current{% endif %}"
              data-media-id="{{ media.id }}"
              data-media-type="video"
              {% if media_colors != blank %}data-colors="{{ media_colors | escape }}"{% endif %}
            >
              {{ media | video_tag: controls: true, preload: 'none', image_size: '800x' }}
            </div>

          {%- when 'external_video' -%}
            <div
              class="gallery-item gallery-item--video gallery-item--embed{% if forloop.first %} is-current{% endif %}"
              data-media-id="{{ media.id }}"
              data-media-type="external_video"
              {% if media_colors != blank %}data-colors="{{ media_colors | escape }}"{% endif %}
            >
              {{ media | external_video_tag }}
            </div>

          {%- else -%}
            {%- comment -%} Stills, and 3D models rendered as their preview still: this
            theme ships no model-viewer, and pulling one in would mean a CDN script —
            the preview image is the honest fallback, and it zooms like any photo.
            The four srcset steps and the sizes string are the LCP mirror. {%- endcomment -%}
            <button
              type="button"
              class="gallery-item{% if forloop.first %} is-current{% endif %}"
              data-media-id="{{ media.id }}"
              data-media-type="{{ media.media_type }}"
              data-zoom-src="{{ media | image_url: width: 1024 }}"
              {% if media_colors != blank %}data-colors="{{ media_colors | escape }}"{% endif %}
              aria-label="{{ 'product.gallery.zoom_image' | t: index: forloop.index }}"
            >
              <img
                src="{{ media | image_url: width: 800 }}"
                srcset="{{ media | image_url: width: 500 }} 500w, {{ media | image_url: width: 640 }} 640w, {{ media | image_url: width: 800 }} 800w, {{ media | image_url: width: 1024 }} 1024w"
                sizes="(max-width: 720px) 80vw, 46vw"
                width="800" height="1200"
                alt="{{ media.alt | default: product.title | escape }}"
                {% if media.id == lcp_media_id %}fetchpriority="high"{% else %}loading="lazy" decoding="async"{% endif %}
              >
            </button>
        {%- endcase -%}
      {%- endfor -%}

      {%- if gal_count == 0 -%}
        {%- assign ph = product.id | modulo: 6 | plus: 1 -%}
        <div class="gallery-item is-current">{{ 'product-' | append: ph | placeholder_svg_tag }}</div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    {%- comment -%} Dot rail. Empty and [hidden] on purpose — theme.js owns both
    the spans and the hidden flag, and it recounts on resize, so a dot row built
    in Liquid would be wrong the moment the viewport crosses 900px (desktop shows
    exactly one slide). aria-hidden because the counter below is the spoken cue;
    two position announcements for one carousel is noise, not access. {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if gal_count > 1 -%}
      <div class="pdp__dots" data-gallery-dots hidden aria-hidden="true"></div>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%} Visually hidden, not shown: with 20+ photos a visible "n / total"
    reads as chrome across the photograph. It is the gallery's only spoken position
    cue. NOTE for whoever wires the next theme.js pass: nothing rewrites this text
    today — the dot sync in initPDP() is the natural place to also set it. {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if gal_count > 0 -%}<p class="visually-hidden" data-gallery-counter aria-live="polite">1 / {{ gal_count }}</p>{%- endif -%}
  </div>
</div>
